{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 5, :comments ["<b>Bread you did not eat and wine and strong drink you did not drink</b>. The sense of לֹא אֲכַלְתֶּם (you did not eat) is: you did not eat of it in a manner that you could sustain yourselves from it, for your primary sustenance was through the manna, in order that you may know that I am YHWH your Elohim, who keeps you alive through miraculous deeds. Its meaning is not that they ate no bread at all, as in לֶחֶם לֹא אָכַלְתִּי וּמַיִם לֹא שָׁתִיתִי (Deuteronomy 9:9), for at certain times Israel did have bread in the wilderness, as written (Deuteronomy 2:28–29), אֹכֶל בַּכֶּסֶף תַּשְׁבִּרֵנִי וְאָכַלְתִּי (Sell me food for silver and I will eat), וּמַיִם בַּכֶּסֶף תִּתֶּן לִי וְשָׁתִיתִי (and give me water for silver and I will drink), כַּאֲשֶׁר עָשׂוּ לִי בְּנֵי עֵשָׂו הַיֹּשְׁבִים בְּשֵׂעִיר וְהַמּוֹאָבִים הַיֹּשְׁבִים בְּעָר (as the children of Esau who dwell in Seir did for me, and the Moabites who dwell in Ar), and our Rabbis mentioned (Yoma 75a) the things that merchants of the nations of the world brought to them in the wilderness. And it is further possible that from the time the manna descended until they came to Seir they ate no bread at all, for they journeyed through the great and terrible wilderness, but in the fortieth year they drew near to civilization and they were told (Deuteronomy 2:4–6), וְאֶת הָעָם צַו לֵאמֹר אַתֶּם עֹבְרִים בִּגְבוּל אֲחֵיכֶם בְּנֵי עֵשָׂו (Command the people, saying: You are passing through the territory of your brothers, the children of Esau), אֹכֶל תִּשְׁבְּרוּ מֵאִתָּם (you may buy food from them), and there (Deuteronomy 29:7) it is written, זֶה אַרְבָּעִים שָׁנָה ה' אֱלֹהֶיךָ עִמָּךְ לֹא חָסַרְתָּ דָּבָר (These forty years YHWH your Elohim has been with you; you have lacked nothing), and from that time the Edomites and the Moabites would set out before them bread and water, and the great men of Israel would buy from them and eat for pleasure, not out of need and not to satiety, and their primary sustenance was through the manna."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 29, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T04:15:41.982709125Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}